{"ref":"BDB Aramaic, דְּכַר","hw":"דְּכַר","html":"† <big>[<span dir=\"rtl\">דְּכַר</span>]</big>  <strong>n.m. ram (</strong>𝔗 <span dir=\"rtl\">דִּכְרָא</span>, Syriac <span dir=\"rtl\">ܕܶܟܪܳܐ</span> id., also (and primarily) <em>male</em>, v. BH <a data-ref=\"BDB, זָכָר\" href=\"/BDB,_זָכָר\", dir=\"rtl\">זָכָר</a><strong>)</strong>;—pl. <span dir=\"rtl\">דִּכְרִין</span> for sacrifice <a data-ref=\"Ezra 6:9\" href=\"/Ezra.6.9\">Ezr 6:9</a>, <a data-ref=\"Ezra 6:17\" href=\"/Ezra.6.17\">17</a>; <a data-ref=\"Ezra 7:17\" href=\"/Ezra.7.17\">7:17</a>.","next":"BDB Aramaic, דִּכְרוֹן","prev":"BDB Aramaic, דִּכֵּן"}